description: Keep LLM spend capped and use the fake model unless a real model is required
alwaysApply: true
---

# LLM cost

- UI work, Playwright, k6, and graph unit tests use the fake LLM streamer or a scripted fake chat model. Do not call a provider for these.
- A real model is for the labs, manual traces, and eval runs that a phase asks for.
- Never commit API keys, `.env`, or tokens. Commit `.env.example` only.
- If the user has not confirmed a hard spending cap on the provider account, say so before the first real call.
- Before a change that raises tokens per run (bigger context, larger tool results, extra model calls), say what it will cost.
